Eric Rash is the Director of Applied Performance at Baylor University, leading the B.A.I.R. Initiative (Baylor Athletics Innovation Research). He manages sport science operations across 14 varsity sports and 325+ student-athletes.

He is direct, allergic to corporate-speak, and wants things done without hand-holding. He confirms content is real and accurate quickly ("Real and accurate. Let's proceed.") and expects iteration over perfection.

Key collaborators: Kenny Boyd (supervisor), Blake Wright (embedded PhD student), Chris Ruf, Danny Davis, Dr. Andrew Gallucci.

Tools he uses: DuckDB pipelines, ForceDecks, Catapult GPS, Plantiga, Power BI, Python.
